# klip-dictionary-data v5 — provenance manifest
#
# Every number here is measured, not carried over. One block per language.
#
# **v5 ADDS THE PACKS THEMSELVES.** v1-v4 published only the gzipped JSONL
# exports and recorded each `.sqlite` pack as an intermediate that was
# deleted. v5 publishes the PACK for every language small enough to ship, and
# records `pack.sha256` and `pack.bytes` for ALL NINETEEN — including the ones
# held back. **EVERY `pack.sha256` FIELD BELOW CARRIES A REAL DIGEST**; none
# is unrecorded, which was v4's regression.
#
# WHY: the Klip app downloads a finished pack at runtime and verifies it
# against this manifest. Building the pack on the device was rejected — it
# would move the whole classifier (D6 classes, the Han rule, the
# primary-sense rule, `dictFold`, the Arabic expansion parse) into the app,
# so a classifier fix would need an app release instead of a data release.
#
# BUILDER      Klip commit 3fe49f16549d623c09235725c8790ff28dabf04d (develop)
#              tool/dict_pack/build_pack.dart
# EXPORTER     export_pack.py in this repo, python3 -I, stdlib only.
# CHAIN        kaikki extract -> Dart pack (.sqlite) -> gzipped JSONL asset
#              The PACK is now a published artifact, not only an intermediate.
#
# ── WHICH PACKS ARE ATTACHED, AND WHY THE OTHERS ARE NOT ─────────────────
#
# Owner ruling 2026-11-06: publish every pack <= 60 MiB; hold the rest until
# the folded-key form dedupe is measured and ruled on. Every held pack's
# size and hash are recorded below so the decision is auditable, and the
# reason is on its own `status` line.
#
#   ATTACHED (7)  da el hi ko nl no zh
#   HELD    (12)  ar de en es fr it ja pl pt ru sv tr
#
# **THE PACK FORMAT IS `pack_format 2`**, recorded in each pack's own `meta`
# table. A consumer reads the format from the pack, never from a filename.
#
# ── ALL NINETEEN EXTRACTS WERE RE-VERIFIED BEFORE THIS BUILD ─────────────
#
# Each extract.sha256 below was recomputed and matched the value v4 recorded.
# The packs came out BYTE-FOR-BYTE THE SAME SIZE as v4's, which is the
# expected result: `tool/dict_pack` is unchanged between v4's builder and
# this one (the only diff is a new `bench.dart`, which `build_pack.dart` does
# not use). The sizes were CONFIRMED against v4, not assumed from it.
#
# ── EVERY PACK WAS HASHED BEFORE ANYTHING WAS DELETED ────────────────────
#
# v4's regression was deleting each intermediate before hashing it, which is
# why its `pack.sha256` was unrecorded. This build hashes the pack as soon
# as it exists, then measures it, and only then deletes the oversized ones.
#

